# Code comments

When adding or editing Python (and similar) code in this repo:

- Prefer `#` one-line comments over `"""` docstrings for modules, classes, and functions/methods.
- Put the `#` comment **immediately above** the module top / `class` / `def`.
- Keep comments to **one short line**; explain *what/why*, not a restatement of the code.
- Korean, noun-style preferred (avoid long `~한다` sentences).
- Do not leave new public helpers uncommented.
